-- CISSP Domain 3 (Security Architecture and Engineering) expansion, part A of 3.
-- Adds flashcards ci-f-800..823 (core), ci-a-280..289 (acronym), ci-y-170..177
-- (feynman), and questions ci-q-800..833, covering 3.1 secure design principles
-- (fail-secure/fail-open, fail-safe defaults, Zero Trust, privacy by design,
-- economy of mechanism, open design, psychological acceptability, separation
-- of privilege vs. separation of duties), 3.2 security models (state machine,
-- information flow, non-interference, Take-Grant, Graham-Denning, plus deeper
-- Bell-LaPadula/Biba/Clark-Wilson/Brewer-Nash nuance beyond the existing basic
-- cards), and 3.3 select controls based on systems security requirements (NIST
-- RMF Select step, SP 800-53B baselines, Common Criteria Protection Profile /
-- Security Target / Target of Evaluation / SFR-SAR, assurance-to-risk matching,
-- compensating controls).


